                <mxCell id="panelCR" value="Catalog invariants" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=3;fillColor=#e8eaf6;strokeColor=#3949ab;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#1a237e;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1500" y="850" width="840" height="340" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="invariants" value="1. Source of truth = repo skills/ (25 dispatchable dirs).  2. install-skills.sh mirrors skills/ into      · ~/.claude/skills/work-intelligence/&lt;name&gt;/      · ~/.claude/skills/&lt;name&gt; (top-level symlink for slash-command)      · ~/.hermes/skills/wi/&lt;name&gt;/ (Hermes flat layout)    Pass --prune to reconcile deletions.  3. skill_catalog table (SQLite) is populated by discoverSkills() at    bridge boot (src/services/cypher/skill-discovery.ts:292).      · UPSERTs every SKILL.md under the scanned roots      · PRUNES rows whose source_path is under a scanned root but        whose file is gone (kill switch: WI_SKILL_DISCOVERY_PRUNE=0)      · Skips dirs starting with `_` (e.g. _TEMPLATE)      · Skips SKILL.md with `dispatchable: false` frontmatter  4. resolveCandidates() in candidates.ts:147 reads the catalog to    build the /wi candidate pool for each dispatch. When the model    picks a name, that name resolves via source_path to a real dir.  Verification: .planning/skill-catalog-cleanup/verify-dispatch- candidates.mjs re-derives the candidate pool from the live DB." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#3949ab;fontColor=#1a237e;fontSize=10;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;verticalAlign=top;" parent="1" vertex="1">
