                    <mxGeometry x="1210" y="120" width="1150" height="1300" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="des_intro" value="Placeholder starter — the user drives what goes here. Suggested framing: what changes about SCOPE would make the model dispatch more reliably? (Group C investigation: 18 of 20 real goals had empty refined_goal.)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;dashed=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#f57c00;fontColor=#e65100;fontSize=10;fontStyle=2;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="170" width="1090" height="60" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="des_slot1" value="DESIRED STEP 1 (edit me)  e.g. &#39;Always run Stage 1 fetch (drop the WI_STAGE1_ENABLED flag). Master-default OFF was a rollout safety; the 60s halt is cured and priors are populated — flip to on by default, remove the branch.&#39;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#f57c00;fontColor=#bf360c;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="250" width="1090" height="90" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="des_slot2" value="DESIRED STEP 2 (edit me)  e.g. &#39;Never write refined_goal=NULL to cypher_sessions when SCOPE returned a parseable brief. Currently 18 of 20 real-user goals in Group C have empty refined_goal — investigate H1 (parse fail) vs H2 (lossy write) per 03-GROUP-C-INVESTIGATION.md.&#39;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#f57c00;fontColor=#bf360c;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="350" width="1090" height="90" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="des_slot3" value="DESIRED STEP 3 (edit me)  e.g. &#39;SCOPE should emit an SSE event with the brief BEFORE handing off to EXECUTE, so the user sees what Cypher understood the goal to be. Today the brief is invisible until session-detail view loads.&#39;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#f57c00;fontColor=#bf360c;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="450" width="1090" height="90" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="des_slot4" value="DESIRED STEP 4 (edit me)  e.g. &#39;When Stage 1 confidence == low AND top_skill is null, halt with asked_user instead of proceeding to EXECUTE. Cheaper than letting the model no-op and mislabeling as success.&#39;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#f57c00;fontColor=#bf360c;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="550" width="1090" height="90" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="des_slot5" value="DESIRED STEP 5 (edit me)  e.g. &#39;refined_goal.evidence_cited must include at least ONE entry with source in {file, ticket, adr}. Empty evidence = SCOPE didn&#39;t actually reason, just pattern-matched. Enforce at validator level.&#39;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#f57c00;fontColor=#bf360c;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="650" width="1090" height="90" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="des_slot6" value="DESIRED STEP 6 (edit me)  e.g. &#39;Deprecate the multi-round path. It&#39;s dead code — Stage 1 single-pass wins on latency (p95 ~6.9s vs ~60s) and never halts. The legacy path only exists for the WI_STAGE1_ENABLED=0 kill switch.&#39;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff3e0;strokeColor=#f57c00;fontColor=#bf360c;fontSize=10;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="750" width="1090" height="90" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="des_slot7" value="DESIRED STEP 7 (add more as needed)  Add / remove / reorder these slots freely. Once we lock the shape, I&#39;ll re-diagram the target state, we&#39;ll audit code against it, then land the deltas as ADRs + commits." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;dashed=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#f57c00;fontColor=#e65100;fontSize=10;fontStyle=2;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="850" width="1090" height="90" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="des_legend" value="How to use this column: 1. Reply with the shape you want (edit any slot&#39;s text or say &#39;add slot for X&#39;). 2. I&#39;ll redraw this column to match. 3. Once locked, we&#39;ll walk left-to-right and file the deltas as work." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff8e1;strokeColor=#f57c00;fontColor=#bf360c;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" parent="1" vertex="1">
